I think setting largestOverlap = TRUE is good for distinguishing the lncRNA reads from the other reads in the total RNA-seq data. If a read has longer overlapping with an actual exon, it is much unlikely from a lncRNA and this can reduce the noise in the counts to the lncRNA regions. To that end, a GTF file mixing lncRNA and exons (like the Ensembl GTF file) is better for the analysis.

